<article class="env-lemma" id="05X3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05X3">Lemma <span data-tag="05X3">76.23.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $Y \to Z$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$ is locally of finite presentation over $Z$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$ is flat over $Z$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$Y$ is locally of finite type over $Z$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ x \in |X| : X\text{ flat at }x \text{ over }Y\} .  \]
</div>
  <p> is open in $|X|$ and its formation commutes with arbitrary base change $Z' \to Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/05X2" data-tag="05X2">76.23.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>